      "hydrogenFilter": "Axial only"
    }
  },
  {
    "title": "Equatorial hydrogens only",
    "narration": "Now only the blue equatorial hydrogens remain, six of them fanning outward around the rim — again three tilted slightly up and three slightly down, alternating.",
    "state": {
      "modelStyle": "Space-filling",
      "hydrogenFilter": "Equatorial only"
    }
  },
  {
    "title": "Open up the model",
    "narration": "The ball-and-stick view shows the same arrangement with the bonds visible. Click any carbon: its red axial and blue equatorial hydrogen light up together — both belong to that one carbon.",
    "state": {
      "modelStyle": "Ball-and-stick",
      "hydrogenFilter": "Both"
    }
  },
  {
    "title": "Compare the two models",
    "narration": "Side by side, the packed and open representations match position for position. Orbit to a side-on view to watch the axial bonds line up parallel to the ring axis while the equatorial bonds point out around the belt.",
    "state": {
      "modelStyle": "Side-by-side",
      "hydrogenFilter": "Both"
    }
  }
]

CAMERA VIEW (framing only). Call setCameraView({ projection, ...these }) AFTER all geometry is added. Keep the projection MECHANISM from PROJECTION TYPE above (orthographic / sheared-oblique / perspective). For perspective these params set the pose (azimuth/elevation/roll); for the two parallel projections pose is a standard default (see PROJECTION TYPE above), and these params set only roll and framing (heightFraction):
{
  "azimuthDeg": 0,
  "elevationDeg": 90,
  "rollDeg": 0,
  "heightFraction": 0.65
}

NOTES: Three.js: MeshPhysicalMaterial (or MeshStandardMaterial with clearcoat-like low roughness ~0.25) plus one key directional light from the upper-left and a soft fill, to reproduce the glossy CPK highlight. Build each atom as a group so filtering just tweens material.opacity (transparent:true) and scale between 1 and 0 rather than removing meshes — keeps counts stable and the fade legible. Raycast only against carbon meshes (ball-and-stick mode) for the click interaction; on select, raise emissive on that carbon plus its paired axial and equatorial H and desaturate/dim all other atoms to ~35% opacity. Space-filling spheres need polygonOffset or slight radius jitter to avoid z-fighting at interpenetration seams; render with depthWrite true and no transparency unless a filter fade is active. Labels and arrows as CSS2DRenderer HTML overlays with SVG arrow paths so they stay crisp and can be pinned to atom screen positions during orbit (hide them once the camera tilts more than ~35° off the axis view). OrbitControls with damping, target at the ring centroid (or midpoint between panels in side-by-side), zoom limited so the figure keeps filling ~65% of the frame.

Follow the interaction plan above.

